{"type":"text","timestamp":1794357754021,"sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","part":{"id":"prt_1c80e7887001mYIEodgUjt2kGP","messageID":"msg_1c80e6ca6001l46qsIEGU30qAq","sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","type":"text","text":"<think>The venv creation outside the workspace is denied (external_directory for /tmp/opencode seems allowed, but the deny rule matched?). It says external_directory /tmp/opencode/* allow, and deny * — hmm the deny came after. Actually the rule list order: allow * for all, allow external_directory *, deny external_directory *. The deny for external_directory * would block /tmp/opencode. But it says /tmp/opencode/* is allowed... confusing. The command failed, maybe because of the venv pip install needing network.\n\nLet me just install python deps into the workspace instead? That would pollute the repo. Alternative: use `pip install --user` or check if flask is already availablesystem-wide.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794357753991,"end":1794357754007}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794357754415,"sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c80e75a4767aad7ea8cf","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"import flask, werkzeug, itsdangerous; print(flask.__version__, werkzeug.__version__, itsdangerous.__version__)\" 2>&1; pip list 2>/dev/null | grep -i -E \"flask|werkzeug|itsdangerous|gunicorn\""},"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask, werkzeug, itsdangerous; print(flask.__version__, werkzeug.__version__, itsdangerous.__version__)\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'flask'\n","metadata":{"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask, werkzeug, itsdangerous; print(flask.__version__, werkzeug.__version__, itsdangerous.__version__)\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'flask'\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 -c \"import flask, werkzeug, itsdangerous; print(flask.__version__, werkzeug.__version__, itsdangerous.__version__)\" 2>&1; pip list 2>/dev/null | grep -i -E \"flask|werkzeug|itsdangerous|gunicorn\"","time":{"start":1794357753999,"end":1794357754382}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c80e788a001XzKnf0vREVXeSJ","sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","messageID":"msg_1c80e6ca6001l46qsIEGU30qAq"}}
