{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794358160315,"sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","part":{"id":"prt_1c814aba6001WesRJRDpuN6fTG","messageID":"msg_1c81476f4001EJMyM2i178tVX9","sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794358160316,"sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","part":{"id":"prt_1c814aba90017pqoT7DyPY65lK","messageID":"msg_1c81476f4001EJMyM2i178tVX9","sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","type":"text","text":"<think>Now let me write a test for the drop math and run it with node (TS type stripping).\n\nTest scenarios (column todo, cards A(1), B(2), C(3), each 100px tall, tops 0, 100, 200):\n\n1. Drag B (fromPosition 2) to the top (pointerY = 10 → above A's midpoint 50): cards excluding B = [A(1, top 0, h 100), C(3, top 200, h 100)]. The pointerY=10 < A.top + 50 = 50 → anchor = A → adjust(A): A.position(1) > fromPosition(2)? No → position = 1 ✓ (B goes to position 1).\n\n2. Drag B to the end (pointerY = 290 → below C's midpoint 250): no anchor → position = adjust(C) + 1 = (C.position 3 > 2 → 3-1 = 2) + 1 = 3 ✓ (B ends at position 3 → order A, C, B).\n\n3. Drag C (fromPosition 3) to the middle between A and B: pointer over B's top half (pointerY = 120; B's midpoint = 150 → 120 < 150 ✓ anchor = B (position 2)); cards excluding C = [A(1, top 0), B(2, top 100)]. adjust(B): B.position 2 > fromPosition 3? No → position = 2 ✓ (C at position 2 → order A, C, B).\n\n4. Drag C to the top (pointerY = 10): anchor = A (position 1) → adjust: 1 > 3? No → position = 1 ✓.\n\n5. Drag A (fromPosition 1) to the end (pointerY = 290): cards excluding A = [B(2, top 100), C(3, top 200)]; no anchor → position = adjust(C) + 1 = (3 > 1 → 2) + 1 = 3 ✓ (A goes to the end → B, C, A).\n\n6. Drag A down to position 2 (between B and C): pointer over C's top half (pointerY = 210; C's midpoint 250 → 210 < 250 → anchor = C (position 3)); adjust(C): 3 > 1 → 2 → position = 2 ✓ (order B, A, C).\n\n7. Cross-column: drag X from in_progress into todo between A and B: pointerY = 120 → cards = [A(1), B(2), C(3)] (all todo cards) → anchor = B (position 2) → status != fromStatus → no adjust → position = 2 ✓.\n\n8. Cross-column to the end: pointerY = 290 → no anchor → position = C.position + 1 = 4 ✓.\n\n9. Empty target column: cards = [] → position 1, index 0 ✓.\n\n10. Drag B onto its own top half (pointerY = 110 — over B's own slot since B occupies 100..200): cards excluding B = [A(top 0), C(top 200)]; pointerY=110 < A.mid(50)? No. < C.mid(250)? Yes → anchor = C (position 3) → adjust: 3 > 2 → 2 → position = 2 ✓ (B stays at 2, no change).\n\nLet me also verify the index values for the indicator: e.g., case 1 → index 0 (the anchor A is at index 0 in the others list) ✓.\n\nLet me write the test file and run it with node.\n\nNode 24 with TS stripping: `node frontend/tests/drop.test.ts`. The import specifier must be \"../src/lib/drop.ts\" (with extension) for node's type stripping to resolve it. Node's type stripping does support importing .ts files with the .ts extension ✓.\n\nLet me write thetest.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794358160297,"end":1794358160311}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794358160342,"sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_01a1c814901575f9920b9113","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"import assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { computeDropTarget } from \"../src/lib/drop.ts\";\nimport type { DropCard } from \"../src/lib/drop.ts\";\n\nconst card = (id: number, position: number, top: number): DropCard => ({\n  id,\n  position,\n  top,\n  height: 100,\n});\n\nlet failures = 0;\n\nfunction check(label: string, actual: unknown, expected: unknown) {\n  try {\n    assert.deepEqual(actual, expected);\n    console.log(`[ok ] ${label}`);\n  } catch {\n    failures += 1;\n    console.log(`[FAIL] ${label} -> got ${JSON.stringify(actual)}, expected ${JSON.stringify(expected)}`);\n  }\n}\n\n// Column todo: A(1) at y 0, B(2) at y 100, C(3) at y 200.\nconst A = card(1, 1, 0);\nconst B = card(2, 2, 100);\nconst C = card(3, 3, 200);\n\n// Drag B (position 2) to the top of the column.\ncheck(\n  \"drag to top\",\n  computeDropTarget({\n    taskId: 2,\n    fromStatus: \"todo\",\n    fromPosition: 2,\n    status: \"todo\",\n    cards: [A, C],\n    pointerY: 10,\n  }),\n  { index: 0, position: 1 },\n);\n\n// Drag B to the bottom of the column.\ncheck(\n  \"drag to bottom\",\n  computeDropTarget({\n    taskId: 2,\n    fromStatus: \"todo\",\n    fromPosition: 2,\n    status: \"todo\",\n    cards: [A, C],\n    pointerY: 290,\n  }),\n  { index: 2, position: 3 },\n);\n\n// Drag C between A and B.\ncheck(\n  \"drag between cards\",\n  computeDropTarget({\n    taskId: 3,\n    fromStatus: \"todo\",\n    fromPosition: 3,\n    status: \"todo\",\n    cards: [A, B],\n    pointerY: 120,\n  }),\n  { index: 1, position: 2 },\n);\n\n// Drag C to the top.\ncheck(\n  \"drag to very top\",\n  computeDropTarget({\n    taskId: 3,\n    fromStatus: \"todo\",\n    fromPosition: 3,\n    status: \"todo\",\n    cards: [A, B],\n    pointerY: 10,\n  }),\n  { index: 0, position: 1 },\n);\n\n// Drag A to the bottom.\ncheck(\n  \"drag first card to bottom\",\n  computeDropTarget({\n    taskId: 1,\n    fromStatus: \"todo\",\n    fromPosition: 1,\n    status: \"todo\",\n    cards: [B, C],\n    pointerY: 290,\n  }),\n  { index: 2, position: 3 },\n);\n\n// Drag A between B and C.\ncheck(\n  \"drag first card down one slot\",\n  computeDropTarget({\n    taskId: 1,\n    fromStatus: \"todo\",\n    fromPosition: 1,\n    status: \"todo\",\n    cards: [B, C],\n    pointerY: 210,\n  }),\n  { index: 1, position: 2 },\n);\n\n// Dropping B on its own slot keeps the position.\ncheck(\n  \"drop on own slot\",\n  computeDropTarget({\n    taskId: 2,\n    fromStatus: \"todo\",\n    fromPosition: 2,\n    status: \"todo\",\n    cards: [A, C],\n    pointerY: 110,\n  }),\n  { index: 1, position: 2 },\n);\n\n// Dragging from another column inserts before the card under the pointer.\ncheck(\n  \"drag in between from other column\",\n  computeDropTarget({\n    taskId: 9,\n    fromStatus: \"in_progress\",\n    fromPosition: 1,\n    status: \"todo\",\n    cards: [A, B, C],\n    pointerY: 120,\n  }),\n  { index: 1, position: 2 },\n);\n\n// Dragging from another column to the end appends.\ncheck(\n  \"drag to end from other column\",\n  computeDropTarget({\n    taskId: 9,\n    fromStatus: \"in_progress\",\n    fromPosition: 1,\n    status: \"todo\",\n    cards: [A, B, C],\n    pointerY: 290,\n  }),\n  { index: 3, position: 4 },\n);\n\n// Dragging from another column to the top.\ncheck(\n  \"drag to top from other column\",\n  computeDropTarget({\n    taskId: 9,\n    fromStatus: \"in_progress\",\n    fromPosition: 1,\n    status: \"todo\",\n    cards: [A, B, C],\n    pointerY: 5,\n  }),\n  { index: 0, position: 1 },\n);\n\n// Empty target column.\ncheck(\n  \"drag into empty column\",\n  computeDropTarget({\n    taskId: 9,\n    fromStatus: \"in_progress\",\n    fromPosition: 1,\n    status: \"done\",\n    cards: [],\n    pointerY: 100,\n  }),\n  { index: 0, position: 1 },\n);\n\n// Filtered view: only the visible cards take part, hidden cards keep their slots.\ncheck(\n  \"drag with filtered column\",\n  computeDropTarget({\n    taskId: 2,\n    fromStatus: \"todo\",\n    fromPosition: 5,\n    status: \"todo\",\n    cards: [card(1, 1, 0)],\n    pointerY: 290,\n  }),\n  { index: 1, position: 2 },\n);\n\nconsole.log(failures === 0 ? \"all drop calculations ok\" : `${failures} failures`);\nprocess.exit(failures === 0 ? 0 : 1);\n","filePath":"/workspace/frontend/tests/drop.test.ts"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/frontend/tests/drop.test.ts","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/tests/drop.test.ts","time":{"start":1794358160306,"end":1794358160319}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c814abac001XSUfYB2bCxJLzx","sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","messageID":"msg_1c81476f4001EJMyM2i178tVX9"}}
