{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794358184536,"sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","part":{"id":"prt_1c8150a41001vK53ZiF3L8Kdrq","messageID":"msg_1c814ecd0001uAFVuIDpVR6rzN","sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794358184536,"sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","part":{"id":"prt_1c8150a43001MlJ7YljLKM5HAp","messageID":"msg_1c814ecd0001uAFVuIDpVR6rzN","sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","type":"text","text":"<think>The full stack works. Now let me verify the frontend renders correctly. Without a browser, I can at least do a server-side render check? Not with Vite/React easily.\n\nHmm, maybe I can use jsdom to render the React app and check the DOM output. That would catch runtime errors (e.g., undefined imports, bad hooks). Let me install jsdom as a devDependency and write a small test that:\n1. Sets up jsdom with the built HTML? The built bundle is an ES module referencing /assets/... which jsdom can't fetch easily (but we can read the files from disk and run them in a jsdom context with a fetch stub).\n\nSimpler approach: use vitest + jsdom + @testing-library/react to render the App with a mocked fetch. That requires installing vitest, jsdom, @testing-library/react — more dev dependencies but they'd be in package-lock (Docker `npm ci` installs devDeps → slower build but fine).\n\nHmm, is it worth it? The main risk in the frontend is runtime errors. A rendering test would catch things like the `drag?.taskId` usage, missing imports, etc.\n\nLet me do a lighter-weight check: install jsdom only (a devDependency) and write a node script that:\n- creates a jsdom window with the built index.html,\n- stubs fetch to proxy to the local server,\n- executes the built JS bundle inside the jsdom context,\n- waits a tick and dumps document.body.innerHTML.\n\nThe built bundle is an ES module (`<script type=\"module\">`), which jsdom doesn't execute (jsdom doesn't support ES modules in scripts). Hmm. But I can build a separate IIFE bundle for testing with esbuild (vite's esbuild): bundle src/main.tsx into a single IIFE file and run it in jsdom.\n\nThat's doable: `npx esbuild src/main.tsx --bundle --format=iife --outfile=/tmp/test-bundle.js --loader:.tsx=tsx --jsx=automatic --define:process.env.NODE_ENV='\"development\"'` — esbuild is available via vite's dependency? Let me check if esbuild is in node_modules (vite depends on esbuild) ✓ probably.\n\nThen in a node script with jsdom:\n- create the DOM, set up globals, stub fetch → proxy to http://127.0.0.1:8000 using node's fetch (with the same-origin URL).\n- run the bundle via vm/jsdom's script execution.\n- check the rendered HTML for expected content (column headers, the auth panel, task cards after creating tasks via the API).\n\nThis gives a real smoke test of the React app. jsdom supports PointerEvent? jsdom doesn't implement PointerEvent (it has MouseEvent). Not needed for the initial render test.\n\nLet me try. First install jsdom as a devDependency.\n\nActually — is jsdom already available? Let me check node_modules. Probably not. Let me install it (devDependency). It's ~a few MB.\n\nLet me do it.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794358184515,"end":1794358184533}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794358210322,"sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c815070a710188a4696d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/frontend && timeout 300 npm install -D jsdom@26.1.0 --no-audit --no-fund 2>&1 | tail -3; ls node_modules/.bin | head -20","timeout":330000},"output":"npm warn deprecated whatwg-encoding@3.1.1: Use @exodus/bytes instead for a more spec-conformant and faster implementation\n\nadded 39 packages in 26s\njiti\nnanoid\nrolldown\ntldts\ntsc\ntsserver\nvite\n","metadata":{"output":"npm warn deprecated whatwg-encoding@3.1.1: Use @exodus/bytes instead for a more spec-conformant and faster implementation\n\nadded 39 packages in 26s\njiti\nnanoid\nrolldown\ntldts\ntsc\ntsserver\nvite\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace/frontend && timeout 300 npm install -D jsdom@26.1.0 --no-audit --no-fund 2>&1 | tail -3; ls node_modules/.bin | head -20","time":{"start":1794358184525,"end":1794358210280}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c8150a46001vWTJDNdAo0LWSY","sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","messageID":"msg_1c814ecd0001uAFVuIDpVR6rzN"}}
