{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794358218427,"sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","part":{"id":"prt_1c8158eaa001lI4qRVZR3HedX2","messageID":"msg_1c8156f0b001cZksXhdsgAPW04","sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794358218427,"sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","part":{"id":"prt_1c8158eaf001k6Q5J0W0yECvRG","messageID":"msg_1c8156f0b001cZksXhdsgAPW04","sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","type":"text","text":"<think>Interesting: vite 8 uses rolldown, not esbuild. Let me check if esbuild is available... The bin list shows jiti, nanoid, rolldown, tsc, tsserver, vite. No esbuild binary. But vite 8 (rolldown-based) can build a library bundle. I can use `npx vite build --config` with a custom config to produce an IIFE/UMD bundle for testing.\n\nLet me create a temporary vite config for the test build:\n```ts\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [react()],\n  build: {\n    lib: { entry: \"src/main.tsx\", formats: [\"iife\"], name: \"App\", fileName: \"test-bundle\" },\n    outDir: \"dist-test\",\n    minify: false,\n  }\n});\n```\nWith lib mode + iife, the CSS is emitted separately (fine).\n\nThen run the bundle in jsdom.\n\nLet me write the test script:\n\n```js\n// tests/render.test.mjs\nimport { JSDOM } from \"jsdom\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\n\nconst bundle = fs.readFileSync(\"dist-test/test-bundle.iife.js\", \"utf8\");\nconst dom = new JSDOM(`<!DOCTYPE html><html><body><div id=\"root\"></div></body></html>`, { url: \"http://localhost:8000/\", pretendToBeVisual: true });\n// stub fetch\ndom.window.fetch = async (input, init) => { ... proxy to node fetch with the base URL ... };\ndom.window.eval(bundle);  // run the IIFE\nawait new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 500));\nconsole.log(dom.window.document.body.innerHTML);\n```\n\nFor fetch: node's global fetch can be used, resolving relative URLs against \"http://localhost:8000/\". The API calls go to /api/... ✓.\n\nNote: the app's `localStorage` — jsdom supports localStorage ✓.\n\nAlso `window.matchMedia` might be needed? Not used.\n\n`document.elementFromPoint` — not used during render.\n\nLet me write this test to verify:\n1. The app renders the three columns with the right labels.\n2. The auth panel is shown for guests.\n3. After registering (simulating the form submit), the username shows.\n\nActually, simulating a React form submit in jsdom is doable: fill the inputs and dispatch a submit event. React 19 attaches events at the root container; dispatching a 'submit' event on the form should trigger React's onSubmit ✓ (React listens for the submit event, which bubbles ✓).\n\nLet me write the test to:\n- render\n- assert the columns/headers exist\n- fill the register form and submit → wait → assert the username appears in the header and the auth panel is gone\n- create a task via the API (directly calling fetch from the test) then reload the board (click?) hmm.\n\nSimplest: after signing in, use the app's own API by dispatching events on the \"New task\" button and the dialog form. That's a full UI test in jsdom! Let me try:\n- Click \"New task\" → the dialog appears → fill title → submit → the card appears in the To Do column.\n\nReact's onClick requires a real MouseEvent dispatch with bubbles: true ✓ (React 19 uses native event delegation at the root).\n\nLet me write it. If it works, it's a strong smoke test.\n\nPotential jsdom issues:\n- `crypto.randomUUID`? Not used.\n- The `IntersectionObserver`? Not used.\n- CSS? Not applied but doesn't matter.\n\nLet me write the test script.\n\nFor the vite lib build, I need to be careful that the lib build doesn't inline CSS imports weirdly — it emits style.css separately, fine.\n\nLet me create the test config andscript.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794358218415,"end":1794358218425}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794358218456,"sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_01a1c815894973b984d08b2e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"import { defineConfig } from \"vite\";\nimport react from \"@vitejs/plugin-react\";\n\n// Builds a single IIFE bundle that can be executed inside jsdom for smoke tests.\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [react()],\n  build: {\n    lib: {\n      entry: \"src/main.tsx\",\n      formats: [\"iife\"],\n      name: \"KanbanApp\",\n      fileName: () => \"kanban-test-bundle.js\",\n    },\n    outDir: \"dist-test\",\n    minify: false,\n    emptyOutDir: true,\n  },\n});\n","filePath":"/workspace/frontend/vite.test.config.ts"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/frontend/vite.test.config.ts","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/vite.test.config.ts","time":{"start":1794358218422,"end":1794358218438}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c8158eb2001NccPwygTWl6Zqc","sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","messageID":"msg_1c8156f0b001cZksXhdsgAPW04"}}
