{"type":"text","timestamp":1794358245688,"sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","part":{"id":"prt_1c815f928001ukdNLcgrf45VRm","messageID":"msg_1c815ea880010FVWuRiXKmYDK5","sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","type":"text","text":"<think>The React development build references `process.env.NODE_ENV`. I need to define `process` in the jsdom window. Let me add `window.process = { env: { NODE_ENV: \"development\" } }` before eval.\n\nAlso for the production build the check would be `process.env.NODE_ENV === \"production\"` → with my stub it's false → it uses the development build ✓ (fine).\n\nLet me set window.process = { env: { NODE_ENV: \"development\" } }.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794358245672,"end":1794358245686}}}
