{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794358259647,"sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","part":{"id":"prt_1c8162fab001SCNcfss8HBv0Ze","messageID":"msg_1c81614350013dYCl0XeIOrxYo","sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794358259647,"sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","part":{"id":"prt_1c8162fae001SZHGP2qKHtVKf7","messageID":"msg_1c81614350013dYCl0XeIOrxYo","sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","type":"text","text":"<think>The registration form submit didn't work. The form submit event was dispatched but React's onSubmit handler probably wasn't triggered, or the request failed.\n\nPossible issues:\n1. React 19 attaches event listeners to the root container. The form is inside the root ✓. Dispatching a 'submit' event on the form should bubble to the root ✓. Hmm, but React's onSubmit for forms... React listens for the \"submit\" event ✓.\n\n2. My `submitForm` sets values via the native setter and dispatches an \"input\" event ✓ (React 19 listens to \"input\" for onChange).\n\nLet me debug: add a check of whether the request was made. Let me print the network calls. Or maybe the issue is that React's event delegation requires the event to be dispatched with `bubbles: true` ✓ which I did.\n\nHmm, another possibility: the submit event handler calls `event.preventDefault()` and then does the async work. If the form fields weren't updated in React state (title empty), the API would return 400 and the error message would show \"Username is required\". The DOM text shows the auth panel still with the form. Let me check if an error message is displayed. The dumped text is truncated. Let me print the full body text on failure.\n\nLet me debug by logging fetch calls in the test.\n\nActually, a likely culprit: React 19 uses `createRoot` and attaches listeners to the root container element. `window.eval(bundle)` renders into `document.getElementById(\"root\")` ✓.\n\nHmm, but does React's synthetic event system require the event target to be within the root container? Yes, it is.\n\nLet me add debugging: log every fetch call with its body and the response status.\n\nLet me modify the test temporarily to print fetch activity.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794358259630,"end":1794358259644}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794358259773,"sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c816270e72e49816105f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/frontend && cat > /tmp/opencode_dbg.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport { JSDOM } from \"jsdom\";\nconst origin = \"http://127.0.0.1:8000\";\nconst bundle = fs.readFileSync(\"dist-test/kanban-test-bundle.js\", \"utf8\");\nconst dom = new JSDOM('<!DOCTYPE html><html><body><div id=\"root\"></div></body></html>', { url: `${origin}/`, pretendToBeVisual: true, runScripts: \"outside-only\" });\nconst { window } = dom;\nwindow.fetch = async (input, init = {}) => {\n  console.log(\"FETCH\", typeof input === \"string\" ? input : input.url, init?.method, init?.body);\n  const url = typeof input === \"string\" ? new URL(input, origin).toString() : input;\n  const res = await fetch(url, init);\n  console.log(\" ->\", res.status);\n  return res;\n};\nwindow.scrollTo = () => {};\nwindow.process = { env: { NODE_ENV: \"development\" } };\nwindow.eval(bundle);\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\nawait sleep(700);\nconst doc = window.document;\nconsole.log(\"forms:\", doc.querySelectorAll(\"form\").length);\nconst form = doc.querySelector(\"form\");\nconst field = form.querySelector('[name=\"username\"]');\nconst setter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(window.HTMLInputElement.prototype, \"value\").set;\nsetter.call(field, \"tester1\");\nfield.dispatchEvent(new window.Event(\"input\", { bubbles: true }));\nawait sleep(100);\nconsole.log(\"input value:\", field.value);\nform.dispatchEvent(new window.Event(\"submit\", { bubbles: true, cancelable: true }));\nawait sleep(800);\nconsole.log(doc.body.textContent.slice(0, 600));\nEOF\ntimeout 120 node /tmp/opencode_dbg.mjs 2>&1 | tail -30","timeout":150000},"output":"node:internal/modules/package_json_reader:331\n  throw new ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND(packageName, fileURLToPath(base), null);\n        ^\n\nError [ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND]: Cannot find package 'jsdom' imported from /tmp/opencode_dbg.mjs\n    at Object.getPackageJSONURL (node:internal/modules/package_json_reader:331:9)\n    at packageResolve (node:internal/modules/esm/resolve:784:25)\n    at moduleResolve (node:internal/modules/esm/resolve:873:18)\n    at defaultResolve (node:internal/modules/esm/resolve:1006:11)\n    at #cachedDefaultResolve (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:705:20)\n    at #resolveAndMaybeBlockOnLoaderThread (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:725:38)\n    at ModuleLoader.resolveSync (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:763:56)\n    at #resolve (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:687:17)\n    at ModuleLoader.getOrCreateModuleJob (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:607:35)\n    at ModuleJob.syncLink (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:276:33) {\n  code: 'ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND'\n}\n\nNode.js v24.22.1\n","metadata":{"output":"node:internal/modules/package_json_reader:331\n  throw new ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND(packageName, fileURLToPath(base), null);\n        ^\n\nError [ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND]: Cannot find package 'jsdom' imported from /tmp/opencode_dbg.mjs\n    at Object.getPackageJSONURL (node:internal/modules/package_json_reader:331:9)\n    at packageResolve (node:internal/modules/esm/resolve:784:25)\n    at moduleResolve (node:internal/modules/esm/resolve:873:18)\n    at defaultResolve (node:internal/modules/esm/resolve:1006:11)\n    at #cachedDefaultResolve (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:705:20)\n    at #resolveAndMaybeBlockOnLoaderThread (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:725:38)\n    at ModuleLoader.resolveSync (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:763:56)\n    at #resolve (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:687:17)\n    at ModuleLoader.getOrCreateModuleJob (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:607:35)\n    at ModuleJob.syncLink (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:276:33) {\n  code: 'ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND'\n}\n\nNode.js v24.22.1\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace/frontend && cat > /tmp/opencode_dbg.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport { JSDOM } from \"jsdom\";\nconst origin = \"http://127.0.0.1:8000\";\nconst bundle = fs.readFileSync(\"dist-test/kanban-test-bundle.js\", \"utf8\");\nconst dom = new JSDOM('<!DOCTYPE html><html><body><div id=\"root\"></div></body></html>', { url: `${origin}/`, pretendToBeVisual: true, runScripts: \"outside-only\" });\nconst { window } = dom;\nwindow.fetch = async (input, init = {}) => {\n  console.log(\"FETCH\", typeof input === \"string\" ? input : input.url, init?.method, init?.body);\n  const url = typeof input === \"string\" ? new URL(input, origin).toString() : input;\n  const res = await fetch(url, init);\n  console.log(\" ->\", res.status);\n  return res;\n};\nwindow.scrollTo = () => {};\nwindow.process = { env: { NODE_ENV: \"development\" } };\nwindow.eval(bundle);\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\nawait sleep(700);\nconst doc = window.document;\nconsole.log(\"forms:\", doc.querySelectorAll(\"form\").length);\nconst form = doc.querySelector(\"form\");\nconst field = form.querySelector('[name=\"username\"]');\nconst setter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(window.HTMLInputElement.prototype, \"value\").set;\nsetter.call(field, \"tester1\");\nfield.dispatchEvent(new window.Event(\"input\", { bubbles: true }));\nawait sleep(100);\nconsole.log(\"input value:\", field.value);\nform.dispatchEvent(new window.Event(\"submit\", { bubbles: true, cancelable: true }));\nawait sleep(800);\nconsole.log(doc.body.textContent.slice(0, 600));\nEOF\ntimeout 120 node /tmp/opencode_dbg.mjs 2>&1 | tail -30","time":{"start":1794358259637,"end":1794358259699}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c8162fb0001bPc9KhAsnqfkZa","sessionID":"ses_e37f28d7bffekBPOL1DKCH4OOV","messageID":"msg_1c81614350013dYCl0XeIOrxYo"}}
